From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arr-optimized <arr-optimized@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] Opt-in lower indexer rate limit and cache-hit refund

Two environment variables, both unset by default (then every request and
grab is paced exactly as on stock):

- ARR_INDEXER_RATE_LIMIT_MS sets the per-indexer request interval for
  indexer types that do not set their own limit (stock: 2000 ms).
- ARR_INDEXER_CACHE_HIT_HEADER (and optionally ARR_INDEXER_CACHE_HIT_VALUE,
  default HIT) names a response header from a caching proxy in front of the
  indexer; a response marked as a cache hit gives its rate-limit slot back.

With a lowered interval, grabs from one host stay at least 2 s apart,
counted from when each grab is released, and the host interval is the last
wait before a grab, so it holds on both sides of the grab.
